export default "import { Meta } from '@storybook/addon-docs/blocks';\n\n<Meta title=\"Docs/Storybook Project Overview\" />\n\n# Raibach Design System Lifecycle Management\n\n> *\"Assemble. Evaluate. Govern.\"*\n\n**Built by Raibach · DeepSeek V4 Pro · v0.4.0-alpha · July 2026**\n\n---\n\n## Curation Rules\n\nThis Storybook is intentionally curated for **AI experience modules**, not a strict atomic design system.\n\n1. Only stories under `src/storybook/**` are loaded.\n2. We showcase **module-level compositions** first — completed UX modules that teams actually consume.\n3. Primitives (buttons, inputs, tokens) exist but are secondary to the browsing model.\n4. Every module story shows **realistic, pull-ready usage** — not toy examples.\n5. Storybook navigation mirrors how product teams **actually assemble AI workflows**.\n\n---\n\n## What We Built\n\nWe didn't build a prompt testing tool. We didn't build a dashboard. We built a **Dynamic Semantic Canvas** — a single, stable interface surface that uses AI as a runtime compiler to serve infinite operational workflows.\n\n**One surface. Any payload. Any user.**\n\n- A field technician types in a hardware model and watches the canvas generate a wiring schematic.\n- A compliance officer queries maritime chemical storage regulations and gets chapter-and-verse from the American Bureau of Shipping.\n- A product manager inputs raw business requirements, selects a Figma design system token set, and watches the AI assemble a production-grade interface from pre-approved atomic components.\n- A UX designer monitors performance telemetry on the same surface, in the same session, without ever leaving the environment.\n\nThe interface never changes. The AI delivers different levels of access, different rendering modes, different output formats — but the human experience remains **cognitively stable**. That's the architecture.\n\n---\n\n## A2UI: The AI Surface Controller\n\nThe AI is not a passive chat widget bolted to the sidebar. It is the **active surface controller** — it reads workspace context, writes to prompt sections, switches tabs, triggers execution, evaluates output, and iterates autonomously until quality thresholds are met.\n\n### Phase 1: Session-Scoped Chat ✅\nEach prompt session owns its conversation. Opening a prompt loads **its** chat history — not a global most-recent thread. Conversations are scoped, versioned, and auditable per session.\n\n### Phase 2: AI Control Tags ✅\nThe AI navigates and executes through XML command tags processed by the frontend:\n\n| Tag | Action |\n|-----|--------|\n| `<update_agent>`, `<update_user>`, `<update_tool>`, `<update_few_shot>`, `<update_context>`, `<update_constraints>` | Write to prompt sections |\n| `<add_role name=\"X\">`, `<remove_role name=\"X\"/>` | CRUD prompt sections |\n| `<switch_tab>trace|variables|chat</switch_tab>` | Navigate right-column tabs |\n| `<run_prompt/>` | Trigger prompt execution |\n| `<show_version>N</show_version>` | Load a version snapshot |\n| `<eval_grounding/>` | Evaluate output against grounding metrics |\n\n### Phase 3: Element ID Layer 🔄\nEvery DOM element the AI touches gets a stable UUID — `data-section-id` on prompt sections, `data-run-id` on execution outputs. IDs persist across saves. The trace tracks changes per element, not per text block.\n\n### Phase 4: Autonomous Loop 🔜\nThe AI sets a goal (`<loop_target>groundedness:0.9</loop_target>`), runs, evaluates, compares to target, edits, re-runs — converging without user intervention. On convergence: notifies the user and stops.\n\n> **Full plan:** [A2UI Control Surface →](./iframe.html?id=docs-a2ui-control-surface--docs)\n\n---\n\n## Architecture: One Surface, Infinite Workflows\n\n### Three-Column Agentic IDE\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  LEFT                    │  THIRD COLUMN         │  RIGHT    │\n│  Prompt Builder          │  Output Workspace     │  AI Chat  │\n│                          │                       │  + Trace  │\n│  ▸ System Role           │  [Model: DeepSeek ▼]  │  + Vars   │\n│  ▸ User Role             │  ┌─────────────────┐  │           │\n│  ▸ Tool Call             │  │                 │  │  Chat:    │\n│  ▸ Few Shot              │  │  Live Output    │  │  scoped   │\n│  ▸ Context               │  │  (editable)     │  │  to this  │\n│  ▸ Constraints           │  │                 │  │  session  │\n│  ▸ + Custom Roles        │  └─────────────────┘  │           │\n│                          │  [Copy] [Save] [Exp]  │  Trace:   │\n│  Drag-and-drop reorder   │  [Regenerate] [Clear] │  Milvus   │\n│  Collapse/expand         │                       │  versions │\n│  File attachments        │  Beforeunload guard   │           │\n│                          │  Locked when active   │  Metrics: │\n│  [Save Template] [RUN ⌘⏎]│  Auto-restore on open │  grounded │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Dual Database\n\n| Database | Purpose |\n|----------|---------|\n| **PostgreSQL** | Sessions, versions, conversations, user data — relational integrity |\n| **Milvus Lite** | Semantic snapshots of every RUN — vector search across execution history |\n\nEvery save creates a timestamped version. Every RUN snapshots to Milvus. The Trace tab merges both into a unified audit trail.\n\n### Atomic Design as Guardrails\n\nThe AI cannot generate arbitrary interfaces. It is structurally constrained by an atomic design system — Brad Frost's atoms, molecules, and organisms mapped to a live Figma token library. If an existing molecule exists, the AI must use it. If the user demands something new, the AI synthesizes from pre-approved atoms.\n\n**Innovation within guardrails. Controlled evolution.**\n\n### The Pipeline\n\n```\nFigma Design ──→ FIGMA_MAKE_PIPELINE ──→ frontend/src/components/\n                                              ↓\nUser builds prompt ──→ SAVE_PIPELINE ──→ PostgreSQL + Milvus\n                                              ↓\nAI controls surface ──→ A2UI_CONTROL_SURFACE ──→ three-column workspace\n```\n\n---\n\n## Feature Status\n\n| Feature | Phase | Status |\n|---------|-------|--------|\n| Section CRUD (AI adds/removes prompt sections) | Now | ✅ Done |\n| AI control tags (tab switch, RUN, version load) | Now | ✅ Done |\n| Grounding metrics in Trace tab | Now | ✅ Done |\n| Element ID layer (UUIDs on DOM elements) | Now | 🔄 In Progress |\n| Session-scoped conversations | Now | 🔄 In Progress |\n| Autonomous loop (AI iterates to threshold) | Next | 🔜 Planned |\n| Save pipeline fix (compiled_output + messages) | Next | 🔜 Planned |\n| Figma Make automation | Next | 🔜 Planned |\n| Role-based access (student/teacher/admin) | Later | 📋 Roadmap |\n| Audit trail (every AI action logged) | Later | 📋 Roadmap |\n| Prompt marketplace (publish/discover agents) | Future | 💡 Vision |\n| CI/CD integration for prompt deployment | Future | 💡 Vision |\n\n> **Full roadmap:** [Roadmap →](./iframe.html?id=docs-roadmap--docs)\n\n---\n\n## Deep Dives\n\n| Document | Content |\n|----------|---------|\n| [A2UI Control Surface](./iframe.html?id=docs-a2ui-control-surface--docs) | Four-phase plan: session chat → control tags → element IDs → autonomous loop |\n| [Architecture Vision](./iframe.html?id=docs-architecture-vision--docs) | The Dynamic Semantic Canvas — one surface, infinite workflows |\n| [Save Pipeline](./iframe.html?id=docs-save-pipeline--docs) | Session persistence: all three columns atomic |\n| [Figma Make Pipeline](./iframe.html?id=docs-figma-make-pipeline--docs) | Design-to-code pipeline: Figma export → transform → flat component structure |\n| [Product Package](./iframe.html?id=docs-product-package--docs) | What it is, who it's for, architecture overview |\n| [Roadmap](./iframe.html?id=docs-roadmap--docs) | Now → Next → Later → Future |\n| [Use Cases](./iframe.html?id=docs-use-cases--docs) | Real human workflows — form fill, grocery order, schematics, therapy, marketplace |\n| [The Magical Third Column](./iframe.html?id=docs-the-magical-third-column--docs) | The infinite canvas — loading anything computable |\n\n---\n\n## Technology Stack\n\n| Layer | Technology |\n|-------|-----------|\n| Frontend | React 19, Vite 7, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS 4, shadcn/ui |\n| Backend | FastAPI (Python 3.14), Uvicorn, PostgreSQL, Milvus Lite |\n| Design-to-Code | Figma Make → custom transform pipeline → flat component structure |\n| Monitoring | Sentry (error boundaries, API tracking, performance profiling) |\n| Deployment | GitHub Actions CI/CD → SiteGround (Apache reverse proxy, PHP proxy layer) |\n| Component Docs | Storybook 8 with Chromatic, a11y addon, interactive testing |\n\n---\n\n## Live Deployment\n\n**Production:** [prompt-portal-prod.raibach.net](https://prompt-portal-prod.raibach.net/)  \n**Storybook:** [prompt-portal-prod.raibach.net/storybook/](https://prompt-portal-prod.raibach.net/storybook/)  \n**GitHub:** [github.com/Raibach/prompt-composer-console](https://github.com/Raibach/prompt-composer-console)\n\n---\n\n*This is the document of record for the Raibach Design System Lifecycle Management project. For hiring managers: this demonstrates a team capable of delivering complex, production-ready applications with deep architectural thinking, AI integration expertise, and design system governance at enterprise scale.*"